<title>USA: Cornerstone Realty says buys two properties.</title>
<headline>Cornerstone Realty says buys two properties.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cornerstone Realty Income Trust said Friday it has bought two properties in the Atlanta area for a total of $29.58 million.</p>
<p>The company said it bought Ashley Run, a 358-unit apartment complex, for $18 million and Carlyle Club, a 243-unit apartment complex, for $11.58 million.</p>
<p>The company said it now owns 46 apartment complexes totaling 10,422 units in Virginia, North Carolina, South Carolina and Georgia.</p>
